`setInterval` keeps running after the last step is reached (it keeps firing even though `currentStep` no longer changes). Consider clearing the interval once `currentStep` hits `LOADING_STEPS.length - 1` (or using a chained `setTimeout`) to avoid unnecessary work while the loading screen stays mounted.
```suggestion
      setCurrentStep((prev) => {
        if (prev >= LOADING_STEPS.length - 1) {
          clearInterval(timer);
          return prev;
        }
        return prev + 1;
      });
```

This uses an inline `style` prop to control opacity. The codebase’s styling approach is Tailwind utility classes (and inline styles are disallowed by the UI architecture guidelines). Please replace this with conditional Tailwind classes (e.g. `opacity-100` / `opacity-30`) so styling stays in className.
```suggestion
                className={`flex items-center gap-2.5 text-sm transition-opacity duration-300 ${
                  index <= currentStep ? 'opacity-100' : 'opacity-30'
                }`}
```
